zoe_cs: FYI — onboarding call w/ Wavelet. After integrating the mobile SDK their beta users saw a sharp spike in 429s that correlated with an analytics batch job. Happened right after they flipped feature-flag to enable event tracking.

rahul_sdk: interesting, are the 429s hitting our /embed or /events endpoints? any sample responses?

zoe_cs: customer pasted a snippet: many 429s to /events/ingest with Retry-After: 0 or omitted. Timeline: user opens app -> analytics worker batches events every 5s -> parallel sent while app also does preflight.

inger_eng: sounds like a mixed-workload surge: telemetry + preflight + model calls. Our per-tenant concurrent request limit doesn't distinguish endpoint type, so analytics bursts can steal capacity.

pat_support: can they throttle analytics client quickly? They said the analytics lib is third-party and bundled in the app, but they can toggle the flag server-side.

rahul_sdk: safe client-side snippet to add queueing/coalescing to the SDK and deprioritize analytics sends: ```js
// queue analytics and send at lower priority
const analytics = new EventBatcher({
  batchIntervalMs: 2000,
  maxInFlightBatches: 1,
  priority: 'low'
});

// in SDK init
const client = new RedwoodSDK({
  maxConcurrentRequests: 6,
  endpointPriority: { events: 'low', preflight: 'high', generation: 'high' },
  retry: { baseMs: 250, maxMs: 4000, jitter: true, respectRetryAfter: true }
});
```

zoe_cs: they can flip the analytics flag but prefer a short-term quota window while they work on the client change.

onboard-bot: Quota change requested by pat_support for tenant wav-520: +60% burst for 4 hours (audit-id: q-2026-1802).

sam_sales: pinging renewal owner — this is early prod ramp, bad experience could affect conversion. If we need >12h of mitigation let's prep an eng session.

inger_eng: two engineering checks: 1) ensure analytics requests are routed to a lower priority pool (we have request tagging but not per-tenant priority split), 2) verify their batching isn't retrying immediately on 429. If batcher sees 429, it should exponentially backoff not re-enqueue immediately.

rahul_sdk: I'll draft a one-page with SDK changes and a snippet for the third-party analytics lib to add 'do-not-retry' tag when server returns 429 with Retry-After. Example: ```js
// on response
if(resp.status === 429){
  const retryAfter = parseInt(resp.headers['retry-after'] || '0', 10);
  if(retryAfter > 0) { suppressEnqueueForMs(retryAfter*1000); }
  else { suppressEnqueueForMs(2000 + Math.random()*800); }
}
```

pat_support: applied temporary bump (onboard-bot confirmed). They're toggling analytics flag now.

zoe_cs: action items: pat -> confirm flag toggle (in progress), rahul -> one-pager + client snippets, inger -> explore priority-tagging feasibility, me -> schedule 30-min watch tomorrow 08:30 PT.

inger_eng: opening INF-3622 to add metrics: tenant.wav-520.events_429_count, tenant.wav-520.concurrent_requests_by_endpoint, and request.priority_hit_rate.

rahul_sdk: ticket INF-3622 created. I'll include suggested SDK defaults for mobile customers and add an example for third-party event libraries.

sam_sales: will join the watch session if UX still degraded. Keep me posted.

zoe_cs: thanks team — moving to follow-up after the watch.
